  "term": "sphingomyelin",
  "definition": "Sphingomyelin is a type of lipid found mainly in the brain and other nervous tissue. It is a sphingolipid with a phosphocholine or phosphoethanolamine head group, which makes it the only sphingolipid class also grouped as phospholipids.",
